<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ion Antonescu</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1882–1946</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Ion Antonescu was a Romanian army officer who ruled <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/romania">Romania</a> as Conducător from 1940 to 1944. Appointed prime minister by Carol II in 1940, he forced the king's abdication, crushed the Iron Guard in 1941 and took Romania into the war against the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/soviet-union">Soviet Union</a> as an ally of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/germany">Germany</a>, while his regime deported and killed hundreds of thousands of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jews">Jews</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/romani-people">Roma</a>. He was arrested in King Michael's coup of August 1944 and executed in 1946.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/ion-antonescu.jpg" alt="Ion Antonescu" width="320" height="454" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown authorUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Ion_Antonescu_1941.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
